# Gold ICT Pro — Phase 9 Architecture Specification
## Institutional Intelligence Engine

**Document status:** Draft for implementation
**Depends on:** Phase 8 (frozen, unmodified)
**Target implementer:** GLM (code generation agent)
**Author role:** Chief Software Architect

---

## 0. Scope and Non-Goals

Phase 9 adds an **enrichment layer** on top of the frozen Phase 8 pipeline. It does not alter, wrap, re-emit, or shadow any Phase 8 contract. Phase 9 modules are strictly **downstream consumers** of Phase 8 outputs.

**In scope:** Multi-Timeframe Structure, Liquidity Hierarchy, Fair Value Gaps, Order Blocks, Breaker Blocks, Premium/Discount Arrays, Market Structure Shift, Confidence Scoring, Trade Rating, Statistics.

**Out of scope:** Any modification to Selection, Structure, Strategy, Arbitration, Recommendation, or Audit modules from Phase 8. Execution, Risk, and Authorization layers are Phase 10+ and are only referenced here as future consumers of Phase 9 outputs.

---

## 1. Inherited Architectural Law (carried forward from Phase 8, non-negotiable)

| Principle | Rule |
|---|---|
| Frozen boundary | Phase 8 modules and contracts are read-only inputs to Phase 9. No Phase 9 module may write into a Phase 8 contract. |
| Single source of truth | Every contract has exactly one writer module. |
| Downstream-only flow | Data flows strictly forward through the dependency graph. No back-references, no cycles. |
| Append-only registries | Any registry-type contract (POI Registry, Institutional Event Log) is append-only; entries are never mutated, only superseded by new versioned entries. |
| Fail-closed propagation | If any upstream `integrity = false`, every downstream Phase 9 module halts output and forwards `integrity = false`. No partial results, no silent defaults. |
| Single responsibility | Each module performs exactly one transformation. Detection, classification, scoring, and logging are always separate modules, never merged. |

