## 4. Data Flow Summary

1. Phase 8 outputs (read-only) enter Phase 9 only through explicit contract reads — never through shared mutable state.
2. MTF Structure Adapter is the sole module permitted to re-invoke Phase 8's Structure Engine across timeframes; every other Phase 9 module receives MTF context only through `MTFStructureContract`.
3. Detection-tier modules (FVG, Order Block, MSS, Liquidity Hierarchy, PD Array) run independently and in parallel — none depends on another detection-tier module except where explicitly noted (Order Block → Breaker Block, MSS → Breaker Block).
4. All detection-tier outputs converge at the POI Aggregator — the only module allowed to write `POIRegistryContract`.
5. Scoring (Confidence Scoring Engine) and grading (Trade Rating Engine) are strictly sequential and each single-purpose: score first, grade second. Grading logic never re-derives a score.
6. All Phase 9 modules emit to the Institutional Event Log; the log is the only module that batches events into the append-only ledger.
7. Audit and Statistics are terminal, read-only, and never feed back into any upstream module (no cycles).

